<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd job for update.sh — fires once a day at a fixed time (StartCalendarInterval),
  same shape as digest-schedule.plist.template. This is how a user finds out something
  changed without checking by hand: update.sh pings a desktop notification when it
  actually pulls new commits, or when it's blocked and needs a human — never on the
  common no-op "already up to date" day.

  setup.sh installs this automatically if you say yes to the update-schedule prompt.
  Manual install, if you skipped that or need a second machine:
    cp update-schedule.plist.template ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.dori.update.plist
    # edit __HOUR__, __MINUTE__, __NODE_PATH__ (output of `command -v node`), and the
    # two __REPO_PATH__/__HOME__ path placeholders
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.dori.update.plist

  To change the time later: edit the Hour/Minute in the installed plist directly, then:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.dori.update.plist
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.dori.update.plist

  Logs: ~/.dori/update.log
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.dori.update</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>__REPO_PATH__/update.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>DORI_NODE_PATH</key>
    <string>__NODE_PATH__</string>
  </dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__REPO_PATH__</string>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>__HOUR__</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>__MINUTE__</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.dori/update.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.dori/update.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
